{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/525208-kindred-city-political-structure-visual-diagram","id":525208,"title":"Kindred City political structure visual diagram","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-23T00:57:47-07:00","id":525208,"title":"Kindred City political structure visual diagram","content":"Maybe I like diagrams too much, or maybe I just need them to get a grasp, anyhow: I've made one for Kindred cities from info I gathered across the VtR line.<br /> <br /> The first has some Masquerade elements (Clan Myrmidons, &quot;Camarilla&quot; Inner Council, Justicars and Archons for my own game), on the second diagram I removed those for others to use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://i57.tinypic.com/t9e2x1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i57.tinypic.com/t9e2x1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i57.tinypic.com/t9e2x1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://i57.tinypic.com/t9e2x1.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://i62.tinypic.com/i4i7bp.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i62.tinypic.com/i4i7bp.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://i62.tinypic.com/i4i7bp.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://i62.tinypic.com/i4i7bp.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i57.tinypic.com/t9e2x1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i62.tinypic.com/i4i7bp.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Of course not all cities are the same. Spymaster is just a suggestion for an &quot;extra&quot; Prince-appointed position. It's just a visual aide to help think our cities.<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: I understand that not everyone adheres to the idea of a &quot;default&quot; or &quot;cookie-cuter&quot; city structure, or reject any reference to VtM, or acknowledge that VtM <i>even had</i> a default structure (a late VtM book suggests other possible arrangements of power). I'm not taking a stance, merely collating information. My own cities are likely to be departures from my own &quot;default&quot;; Boston will be ruled by a Council of would-be Princes, Portsmouth, Portland or Providence wouldn't have all the Clans/Covenants on the chart, and New York would have a bloated-byzantine power structure reflecting the extreme overpopulation of 600+ Kindred. A Carthian-run city wouldn't likely have a full-fledged Invictus Inner Circle, etc. Some cities could even actually not be acknowledged as cities &quot;proper&quot; by their neighbors and be considered territories up-for-grabs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5602,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","user":"BarbeChenue","date":". 05-23-2015, 04:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T11:32:41-07:00","id":527906,"title":"","content":"I think it is great that you put together an organizational chart for this. I fully intend to use this as a reference when explaining how offices relate to one another, especially helpful for new players, I think. Sometimes, you just have to draw it. Thank you for sharing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3054-valkys","name":"Valkys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T06:53:56-07:00","id":528759,"title":"","content":"I'll probably add a few more, like Herald, as well as those that were suggested in City of the Damned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T08:37:19-07:00","id":528795,"title":"","content":"Damnation City has a few charts depicting different governing systems of vampire domains with different political setups and alliances.<br /> <br /> Like so.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://data.archive.moe/board/tg/image/1389/49/1389495114953.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-2